# The cases of faults_toml.anti: a name and the value of ANTI_FAULT, see
# tests/CMakeLists.txt. alloc counts the memory of the runtime after the
# start, which the reader takes from the fifth on: the document, the
# copies of the keys and the values, the list of pairs and the names of the
# tables, in the order of the text. The 15th is a pair the inline table
# adds. The second document takes the 20th to the 26th, and its second
# `[[item]]` header the table of the names of the paths with the 24th.
memory_5 alloc:5:ENOMEM
memory_6 alloc:6:ENOMEM
memory_7 alloc:7:ENOMEM
memory_8 alloc:8:ENOMEM
memory_9 alloc:9:ENOMEM
memory_10 alloc:10:ENOMEM
memory_11 alloc:11:ENOMEM
memory_12 alloc:12:ENOMEM
memory_15 alloc:15:ENOMEM
names_memory alloc:24:ENOMEM
